00:15:45.080 --> 00:15:46.570
Miya-chan, wait a second.

00:15:47.520 --> 00:15:49.920
Snacks that come with toys don't count.

00:15:55.460 --> 00:15:57.150
We got quite a bit.

00:15:57.890 --> 00:15:59.130
It's heavy.

00:15:59.130 --> 00:16:00.760
Sorry...

00:16:03.370 --> 00:16:08.570
It you swing something heavy forward,
the momentum will make it easier to walk.

00:16:09.010 --> 00:16:10.630
Swing it?

00:16:11.540 --> 00:16:13.870
Wow!

00:16:15.480 --> 00:16:16.810
Whoa...

00:16:16.810 --> 00:16:18.440
What are they doing?

00:16:21.550 --> 00:16:24.650
Freshmen! Congratulations on
your acceptance!

00:16:24.650 --> 00:16:26.950
We look forward to working with you!

00:16:28.020 --> 00:16:29.460
Cheers!

00:16:35.470 --> 00:16:40.230
How was the entrance ceremony?
Sae was worried about you.

00:16:40.700 --> 00:16:43.440
You were really nervous this morning.

00:16:43.440 --> 00:16:46.640
Yeah, I'm relieved that things went well.

00:16:47.040 --> 00:16:48.340
What about Miya-chan?

00:16:48.340 --> 00:16:50.510
She fell asleep halfway through the ceremony.

00:16:51.150 --> 00:16:54.240
The principal's face and speech were too long.

00:16:55.290 --> 00:16:57.020
Isn't it surprising?

00:16:57.020 --> 00:16:59.050
And he trembled a lot.

00:16:59.460 --> 00:17:02.360
That reminds me of our entrance ceremony.

00:17:02.360 --> 00:17:05.420
I believe Sae was a little late.

00:17:05.900 --> 00:17:07.730
Really?

00:17:07.730 --> 00:17:11.600
Oh, I was with Natsume before the ceremony.

00:17:11.600 --> 00:17:12.800
Natsume?

00:17:12.800 --> 00:17:18.370
Yeah, Natsume mixed up Group A's shoe
compartments with Group B's.

00:17:18.370 --> 00:17:22.150
Come to think of it, we were able
to talk normally back then.

00:17:22.150 --> 00:17:24.980
She didn't always act like that
towards you, did she?

00:17:24.980 --> 00:17:26.610
Hmm...

00:17:27.220 --> 00:17:28.840
Oh well!

00:17:29.690 --> 00:17:32.360
Is there someone named Natsume?

00:17:32.360 --> 00:17:34.520
It's nothing.

00:17:34.520 --> 00:17:36.990
So, what group did the two of you wind up in?

00:17:37.390 --> 00:17:38.630
Group A.

00:17:38.630 --> 00:17:41.760
Miya-chan and I are in the same class.

00:17:42.170 --> 00:17:44.570
We got to sit next to each other too.

00:17:44.570 --> 00:17:46.700
Oh? That's great.

00:17:46.700 --> 00:17:51.000
Yeah! I feel confident with
someone I know with me.

00:17:51.980 --> 00:17:54.740
That means you'll be on the same
team during field day.

00:17:55.140 --> 00:17:56.780
Is that so?

00:17:56.780 --> 00:17:58.920
You're divided into teams by class.

00:17:58.920 --> 00:18:00.750
We were also in Group A.

00:18:00.750 --> 00:18:02.890
Wow, that's great.

00:18:02.890 --> 00:18:06.820
Our homeroom teacher is a woman
by the name of Yoshinoya.

00:18:11.330 --> 00:18:14.020
She's kind of an odd teacher.

00:18:15.500 --> 00:18:17.330
Which means...

00:18:17.330 --> 00:18:20.130
It looks like we'll have a different
homeroom teacher.

00:18:22.740 --> 00:18:26.270
Y-You're right! She's a little odd.

00:18:27.540 --> 00:18:30.440
She said that she'd pose nude if we asked.

00:18:32.880 --> 00:18:33.450
Is that all right?

00:18:33.450 --> 00:18:35.590
They'll learn sooner or later.
Is that all right?

00:18:35.590 --> 00:18:37.920
We don't need to force any opinions
about her onto them.

00:18:43.730 --> 00:18:45.260
That's amazing! How beautiful.

00:18:45.260 --> 00:18:47.460
What kind of snack commercial is this?

00:18:47.460 --> 00:18:48.500
Wow!

00:18:48.500 --> 00:18:50.300
I see you blow it up yourself.

00:18:50.300 --> 00:18:51.300
It expanded!

00:18:51.300 --> 00:18:52.300
Wow!

00:18:52.300 --> 00:18:54.040
It looks good when it's mixed up.

00:18:54.040 --> 00:18:56.110
Is it on sale?

00:18:56.110 --> 00:18:58.040
I didn't see it at Beri-mart.

00:18:58.510 --> 00:19:00.600
Hiro, I see you're keeping an eye out for it!

00:19:01.210 --> 00:19:02.650
It ended.

00:19:02.650 --> 00:19:04.440
Let's buy it next time.

00:19:07.680 --> 00:19:09.190
Do you need a juice refill?

00:19:09.190 --> 00:19:11.180
Th-Thank you very much.

00:19:11.950 --> 00:19:14.520
Your room is very nice, Hiro.

00:19:14.520 --> 00:19:15.730
You think so?

00:19:15.730 --> 00:19:18.490
Your wallpaper seems very new.

00:19:20.030 --> 00:19:26.100
Oh, Room 103 and 203 are empty, aren't they?

00:19:26.100 --> 00:19:30.330
I wonder if we can use them to store things?

00:19:31.640 --> 00:19:32.840
No way!

00:19:32.840 --> 00:19:34.640
You'll get scolded if you go in.

00:19:34.640 --> 00:19:37.340
The landlady here is very scary.

00:19:38.080 --> 00:19:39.080
Okay...

00:19:39.080 --> 00:19:40.450
Is that so?

00:19:40.450 --> 00:19:41.850
Yes!

00:19:41.850 --> 00:19:43.480
Is she scary?

00:19:46.160 --> 00:19:48.520
Thank you very much for today.

00:19:48.520 --> 00:19:50.260
Thanks for everything.

00:19:50.260 --> 00:19:51.630
No problem.

00:19:51.630 --> 00:19:55.900
When we moved in, we got
a welcoming party too.

00:19:55.900 --> 00:19:58.770
It's a Hidamari Apartments tradition.

00:19:58.770 --> 00:20:01.170
We've got to be nice to our juniors.

00:20:02.440 --> 00:20:05.040
I've got to get ready for tomorrow.

00:20:05.040 --> 00:20:06.910
Did you unpack your things?

00:20:06.910 --> 00:20:08.710
Yes, most of it.

00:20:08.710 --> 00:20:11.280
I didn't bring that many things.

00:20:11.280 --> 00:20:13.840
Well, you can get things you need here.

00:20:14.520 --> 00:20:15.590
Oh yeah!

00:20:15.590 --> 00:20:18.790
What do all of you do about meals?

00:20:18.790 --> 00:20:20.420
We cook our own.

00:20:20.420 --> 00:20:22.980
We don't eat out very often.

00:20:23.530 --> 00:20:27.460
I see, I guess I should have
some rice sent over.

00:20:28.030 --> 00:20:30.360
You can get that from
Dada-mart for pretty cheap.

00:20:30.730 --> 00:20:32.070
Dada?

00:20:32.070 --> 00:20:34.170
It's the supermarket past Beri-mart.

00:20:34.170 --> 00:20:35.240
Oh?

00:20:35.240 --> 00:20:37.210
Let's go there tomorrow.

00:20:37.210 --> 00:20:38.070
Okay!

00:20:38.070 --> 00:20:41.440
Hiro, I'm jealous you can make anything.

00:20:42.310 --> 00:20:44.380
I ended up learning a lot of recipes

00:20:44.380 --> 00:20:49.820
while trying to keep Sae from
getting malnourished.

00:20:49.820 --> 00:20:51.150
I see...

00:20:51.150 --> 00:20:54.820
I didn't really cook much at home.

00:20:55.560 --> 00:20:58.330
Could you teach me how to make things?

00:20:58.330 --> 00:20:59.630
Of course!

00:20:59.630 --> 00:21:01.300
Yunocchi!

00:21:01.300 --> 00:21:05.570
Try to learn how to make lots
of delicious dishes!

00:21:05.570 --> 00:21:07.070
Okay! I'll try my best!

00:21:07.070 --> 00:21:10.100
All right, now I don't have
to worry about food.

00:21:10.510 --> 00:21:12.130
Hey!

00:21:15.980 --> 00:21:19.110
I wonder what Miya-chan is going to
do about sketching tomorrow?

00:21:31.290 --> 00:21:33.000
Huh?

00:21:33.000 --> 00:21:34.630
Hiro?

00:21:34.630 --> 00:21:37.600
I wonder if she had business
with Miya-chan?

00:21:39.270 --> 00:21:41.100
Miya-chan!

00:21:41.100 --> 00:21:42.670
Coming!

00:21:42.670 --> 00:21:44.660
What is it? What's wrong?

00:21:44.770 --> 00:21:46.400
Oh, Miya-chan...

00:21:55.220 --> 00:21:57.210
I was really nervous today.

00:21:58.350 --> 00:22:01.550
After I'm done taking a bath, I'll call Mom.

00:22:03.860 --> 00:22:05.760
I'm looking forward to tomorrow!

00:22:06.800 --> 00:22:09.770
April 7
The End
To Be Continued

00:22:19.240 --> 00:22:25.550
An unknown world stretched out

00:22:25.550 --> 00:22:31.280
Connecting, endless connecting threads

00:22:31.920 --> 00:22:38.330
An upside down world is pretty fun

00:22:38.330 --> 00:22:44.130
Connecting, never-ending threads

00:22:44.500 --> 00:22:50.200
You are smiling somewhere today

00:22:50.740 --> 00:22:55.780
I will run all night until the day we meet again

00:22:55.780 --> 00:22:57.380
Run all night

00:22:57.380 --> 00:23:00.450
The record of a resounding shooting star

00:23:00.450 --> 00:23:03.790
Your singing voice

00:23:03.790 --> 00:23:06.860
Touches my heart

00:23:06.860 --> 00:23:10.130
A sky full of shooting stars

00:23:10.130 --> 00:23:13.260
The record of a shining shooting star

00:23:13.260 --> 00:23:16.470
Your whispering voice

00:23:16.470 --> 00:23:19.900
Leads me through space

00:23:19.900 --> 00:23:22.770
A song about shooting stars

00:23:22.770 --> 00:23:26.310
I can't hear them

00:23:26.310 --> 00:23:30.250
I can't reach them

00:23:30.250 --> 00:23:34.810
The footsteps I'm looking for

00:23:40.070 --> 00:23:41.500
Preview

00:23:41.500 --> 00:23:44.440
Preview
Do you have any music that
makes you feel like running?

00:23:44.440 --> 00:23:47.310
Preview
I do! I also have music for entrances,
music for trading places,

00:23:47.310 --> 00:23:48.910
Preview
music for exits and music for relay races!

00:23:48.910 --> 00:23:51.250
Preview
I'm not sure I entirely understand.

00:23:51.250 --> 00:23:52.750
Preview
In short, it's one of those things, right?

00:23:52.750 --> 00:23:53.680
Preview
That's right! One of those!

00:23:53.680 --> 00:23:57.650
Preview
The usual choices are Heaven and Hell,
Csikós Post, and William Tell.

00:23:57.650 --> 00:24:01.060
Preview
I feel like dancing when I listen to samba.

00:24:01.060 --> 00:24:05.260
Preview
The next episode is
"October 13, The King of the Mountain"

00:24:05.260 --> 00:24:06.930
Preview
We'll be waiting at Yamabuki High School.

00:24:06.930 --> 00:24:08.930
Preview
Be sure to tune in!

00:24:08.930 --> 00:24:09.990
Preview
